+--
+--   The Ambush object  lives inside the Game object at +0x265c8 (REPENTOGON v1.9.7.12 has +0x25b40). Found from the game's
+--                      own callers: every call of Ambush::StartChallenge (0x00833420) is made with `ecx = game + 0x265c8`
+--                      (the room-clear code at 0x006e3a7f, the boss-rush start at 0x006edf4b, ...).
+--   Fields (this+)     0x18 maximum boss-rush waves (a boss-rush count: the Update function 0x00834350 compares it with the wave),
+--                      0x1c bosses per wave (SpawnBossrushWave loops on it), 0x20 active (byte, StartChallenge sets it to 1 and
+--                      does nothing when it is already set), 0x24 current wave (StartChallenge zeroes it), 0x28 a countdown
+--                      (StartChallenge sets 30).
+--   Functions          StartChallenge __thiscall, plain `ret`, 0x00833420 (read from the epilogue 0x008335fa).
+--                      SpawnWave       __thiscall, plain `ret`, 0x00833600 (the one that calls GetRandomRoom, 0x82c7d0).
+--                      SpawnBossrushWave __thiscall, plain `ret`, 0x00833c40 (matches REPENTOGON's signature; epilogue 0x00834348).
+--                      REPENTOGON's signatures for StartChallenge and SpawnWave do not match this build's bytes; the addresses
+--                      come from the disassembly (the first by its field writes, the second by its GetRandomRoom call).
+--   Maximum waves      of a challenge room (3) and of a boss challenge room (2) are not game fields: the Update function computes
+--                      them from the room's subtype (2 for subtype 1, else 3). So the getters answer those constants, as
+--                      REPENTOGON's own do until a mod sets them; the setters are not provided (the game would not follow them).
+--   GetCurrentWave    is 0 when no ambush runs (the global must exist all the time).
+--
